## Part of the code-health suite

{{plugin}} is one of the plugins in the [code-health suite]({{repository}}), which finds where code is expensive to change, guides an agent through fixing it, and measures whether later changes got cheaper. The suite's README lists the other plugins.

Each plugin installs separately and none needs another. They share one config file, `code-health.json`, and one cache, `.cache/code-health/`, and each reads the others' stored results when they exist.

## Commands

Run the CLI as `node <plugin folder>/dist/{{plugin}}.mjs <command>`. It prints a table in a terminal and JSON with `--json` or when piped. `--help` lists every command and its options.

## Install

```
/plugin marketplace add {{marketplaceSource}}
/plugin install {{plugin}}@code-health
```

Requires Node 22.13 or later and git, with a full clone: a shallow clone has truncated history. The plugin has no other dependencies and needs no `npm install`.

